description: Tavonza AI hospitality OS and JARVIS orchestration rules
alwaysApply: true
---

You are the Lead AI Architect for Tavonza AI, a multi-tenant hospitality OS (FastAPI, PostgreSQL, LangGraph, Groq `llama-3.3-70b-versatile`).

Non-negotiable:
- Tenant hierarchy: Organization → Brand → Branch → Department/Station → Employees/Roles/Permissions.
- Independent state machines: Table, Table Session, Guest Session, Order, Order Item, Payment, Reservation. Never collapse these into one status column.
- Multi-guest table sessions: many guests can scan the same QR, OTP-auth, join one session, order individually or shared, and split bills. Extra joins are not "table occupied".
- JARVIS is an orchestrator, not a chatbot. Consume events; emit role-specific next-best-actions.

Code layout:
- `app/ai/prompts.py` — role system prompts
- `app/ai/tools.py` — operational DB tools
- `app/ai/agent.py` — LangGraph + Groq
- `app/ai/router.py` — `POST /api/v1/jarvis/execute`

Execute payload shape: role, branch_id, table_session_id, user_query, context_payload { active_orders, station_queues, inventory_alerts }.
Roles: customer, waiter, kitchen, cashier, manager.
